# 1986 machine ROMs
#
# Drop the machine ROM images into this directory (or point --rom at a
# directory that holds them) and the emulator loads them by name. A full
# C128DCR set is two 32K dumps:
#
#   kernal.bin   0x4000 bytes — KERNAL + EDITOR + Z80-BIOS (VICE-split)
#                 from the C128DCR ROM chip (e.g. MAME 318022-02.u34):
#                   [0x0000..0x0FFF]  EDITOR    -> $C000-$CFFF
#                   [0x1000..0x1FFF]  Z80-BIOS  -> $D000-$DFFF (CP/M)
#                   [0x2000..0x3FFF]  KERNAL    -> $E000-$FFFF
#   basic.bin    0x4000 bytes — BASIC 7.0 low + high halves
#                 from the C128DCR ROM chip (e.g. MAME 318023-02.u32):
#                   [0x0000..0x3FFF]  BASIC low -> $4000-$7FFF
#                   [0x4000..0x7FFF]  BASIC high-> $8000-$BFFF
#   chargen.bin  0x1000 bytes — the C128 character generator (optional)
#
# These ROMs are copyright Commodore and are not redistributed here. Obtain
# them from a source you are entitled to use (for example by dumping your own
# machine or using a MAME/VICE set). The emulator runs and renders its test
# pattern without them.
#
# Current status: the 8502 core executes the reset vector and runs into the
# C128 memory space (it reaches BASIC's address area), but a stable boot
# needs the full VICE 8502 core and the real C128 MMU banking — see
# DEVELOPMENT.md.
